{"benchmark": "livebench_selected", "task_id": "zebra_puzzle:fe37c4db2b25d85eb28bc39dc6c978c002216c9e26227d7a9389abad0dd230f0", "sample_idx": 38, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Let's denote person 1 as P1 and person 2 as P2. We are given the following attributes: Movie-Genre, Pet, Transport, with possible values crime, animation, ferret, lizard, tram, jet-ski.\n\n1. \"The person who watches animation is on the immediate right of the person who has a ferret.\" This means if P1 has a ferret, then P2 watches animation. If P2 has a ferret, then P1 watches animation.\n\n2. \"The person who watches crime is on the immediate left or immediate right of the person who travels by jet-ski.\" This means if someone watches crime, then someone travels by jet-ski is next to them.\n\nLet's analyze the possibilities.\n\nCase 1: P1 has a ferret. Then P2 watches animation.\nSince P2 watches animation, P1 cannot travel by jet-ski because P2 must be next to the person who travels by jet-ski. Therefore, P1 must travel by tram.\nIf P1 travels by tram, then P2 must travel by jet-ski.\nSo, P1: ferret, tram; P2: animation, jet-ski.\nThis satisfies both conditions.\n\nCase 2: P2 has a ferret. Then P1 watches animation.\nSince P1 watches animation, P2 cannot travel by jet-ski because P1 must be next to the person who travels by jet-ski. Therefore, P2 must travel by tram.\nIf P2 travels by tram, then P1 must travel by jet-ski.\nSo, P1: jet-ski, animation; P2: ferret, tram.\nThis satisfies both conditions.\n\nNow let's determine the answers to the questions.\n\n1. What is the movie genre of the person who has a ferret?\nIn Case 1, P1 has a ferret. So, the person who has a ferret is P1, and their movie genre is unknown. In Case 2, P2 has a ferret. So, the person who has a ferret is P2, and their movie genre is animation.\nSince we have unique values for each attribute, we can determine the movie genre.\nIn Case 1, P1: ferret, tram; P2: animation, jet-ski. So, P1's movie genre is unknown and P2's movie genre is animation.\nIn Case 2, P1: jet-ski, animation; P2: ferret, tram. So, P1's movie genre is animation and P2's movie genre is ferret.\nSince we know each person has a unique value for each attribute, and we know that P1 and P2 are different, we can conclude that the person who has a ferret is P2 and their movie genre is animation.\n\n2. What movie genre does the person in position 2 watch?\nIn Case 1, P2 watches animation.\nIn Case 2, P2 watches animation.\nSo, the person in position 2 watches animation.\n\n3. What transport does the person in position 2 use?\nIn Case 1, P2 uses jet-ski.\nIn Case 2, P2 uses tram.\nSince each person has a unique value for each attribute, we can conclude that the person in position 2 uses jet-ski.\n\n4. What transport does the person who has a ferret use?\nIn Case 1, P1 has a ferret and uses tram.\nIn Case 2, P2 has a ferret and uses tram.\nSince each person has a unique value for each attribute, we can conclude that the person who has a ferret uses tram.\n\nFinal answer: animation, animation, jet-ski, tram.\n<solution>animation, animation, jet-ski, tram</solution>", "logprobs": [{"token": "Let", "logprob": -0.0008122005965560675}, {"token": "'", "logprob": -0.04723476245999336}, {"token": "s", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁denote", "logprob": -1.1715691089630127}, {"token": "▁person", "logprob": -1.2782738208770752}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": -1.156323378381785e-05}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁as", "logprob": -0.005403555929660797}, {"token": "▁P", "logprob": -1.2874520507466514e-05}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁and", "logprob": -9.536697689327411e-06}, {"token": "▁person", "logprob": -2.7656173188006505e-05}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "2", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁as", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁P", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "2", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -2.8013790142722428e-05}, {"token": "▁We", "logprob": -1.2387409210205078},